sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Administrator
    actor U as Patient<br/>(identity owner)
    participant G as Gatekeeper<br/>(off-chain data holder)
    participant SC as Smart contracts
    actor R as Provider<br/>(requester)

    A->>SC: setRequesterStatus(provider, true)
    U->>U: Hash the ID files locally (SHA-256)
    U->>G: Store the ID files (front, back)
    U->>SC: registerUser(emailHash, gatekeeper link, frontHash, backHash)
    U->>SC: setConsent(provider, scope, 30 days)
    SC-->>U: 10 ACT reward (first grant to this provider only)
    R->>SC: requestAccess(patient)
    Note over SC: Callers that aren't whitelisted revert
    alt consent valid
        SC->>SC: Log GRANTED, emit AccessGranted
        R->>G: Transaction hash + signature
        G->>SC: Check receipt, whitelist, consent, recency
        G-->>R: Only the files the scope allows
        R->>R: Re-hash files, compare with on-chain hashes
    else consent missing, revoked or expired
        SC->>SC: Log DENIED with reason, emit AccessDenied
        SC-->>R: granted = false, no data
    end
    U->>SC: revokeConsent(provider)
    Note over G,R: From now on: DENIED (REVOKED) on-chain,<br/>and the gatekeeper refuses old transactions
